WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.230
A dark take on the Archie comics, CW's Riverdale
helped launch the careers of a number of new

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.900
stars when it debuted in early 2017.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.660
It's also provided a new home for some big-name
talent who've largely disappeared from Hollywood.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.820
From the show's central cast of angsty teens
to its supporting 90s heartthrobs and heathens,

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.250
these actors have been collectively racking
up credits for a while now, and some of their

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.040
former projects just might surprise you.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.920
Here's why the cast of Riverdale looks so
familiar.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:27.940
KJ Apa

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.980
Riverdale's resident ginger pretty boy Archie
Andrews might seem like the all-American type

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.090
— but he's actually portrayed by dark-haired,
New Zealand-born KJ Apa.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.090
Pretty crazy, huh?

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:42.330
Apa got his start in his home country on the
soap opera Shortland Street, appearing in

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.360
46 of the show's thousands of episodes as
the angsty teen Kane Jenkins.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.170
Apa also briefly appeared in the New Zealand
sci-fi series The Cul De Sac before landing

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.220
a part as a young Dennis Quaid in the controversial
film A Dog's Purpose.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.160
Lili Reinhart

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.220
Lili Reinhart, who plays Betty, Riverdale's
token ponytailed blonde, got her start in

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.240
acting in the drama short For Today in 2010.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.640
Following an appearance on Law and Order:
SVU, she returned to film as the title character

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.100
in the horror flick Lilith and the 2012 drama
short The Most Girl Part of You.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.220
2013 was a huge year for her: She starred
in The Kings of Summer, the baseball mystery

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:21.959
Gibsonburg, and the thriller Forever's End.

00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:27.320
In 2014, Reinhart snagged a recurring role
on the Fox mid-season comedy Surviving Jack,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.820
which was canceled after one season.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.520
Then came Riverdale in 2017, and the rest
is history.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.600
Cole Sprouse

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.000
Child actor Cole Sprouse was probably the
most famous of Riverdale's young actors when

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.420
he was cast as Archie's BFF Jughead.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.099
Sprouse said he was drawn to Jughead because
he was so different from his well-known Disney

00:01:45.099 --> 00:01:49.149
Channel character, Cody Martin, whom he'd
played for eight years in The Suite Life of

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:51.860
Zack and Cody and its spin-off The Suite Life
on Deck.

00:01:52.169 --> 00:01:56.480
Sprouse already had a lot of acting experience
when he signed on to the Suite Life universe.

00:01:56.489 --> 00:02:00.779
The Sprouse twins started acting in 1993 when
they were just 1-year-olds in Chuck Lorre's

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.800
Grace Under Fire.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.140
The Sprouse twins also appeared in the Adam
Sandler film Big Daddy.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.300
"Kangaroo song!"

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.260
"Kangaroo song!"

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:08.620
"Kangaroo song!"

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.920
"Kangaroo song!"

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.740
"ALRIIIIIIGHT!"

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.980
Meanwhile, Cole — without his brother — struck
TV gold when he played Ross' son Ben on iconic

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:18.920
sitcom Friends.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.300
Camila Mendes

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.980
Newcomer Camila Mendes was the least experienced
of Riverdale's teens when she signed on to

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:30.349
play the socialite Veronica Lodge — but
she's quickly proven her acting prowess.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:35.379
Mendes graduated from NYU's Tisch School of
the Arts in May of 2016, just a few months

00:02:35.379 --> 00:02:37.300
after she landed the part of Veronica.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.700
Her only other previous acting credit was
in a commercial for IKEA.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.040
Although Mendes might not be recognizable
from her time before the show, she's blown

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.600
up since season one kicked off, even nabbing
more than 1 million followers on Twitter and

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.330
7 million followers on Instagram.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.500
That's what we call a success story!

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.280
Casey Cott

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:01.140
Casey Cott plays Betty's BFF Kevin on Riverdale,
and while he seems right at home on the small

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.380
screen, most of Cott's pre-Riverdale experience
came in local theater.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.980
Cott's on-screen acting experience was pretty
limited before Riverdale — he appeared in

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:13.540
an episode of Law and Order: SVU and starred
in the music video for Sabrina Carpenter's

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.040
"Why."

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.120
Cott must've really wanted a part on Riverdale
when the show came around, auditioning for

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.000
Archie and Jughead before landing the role
of Kevin.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.240
Madelaine Petsch

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.060
The red-headed Madelaine Petsch was actually
auditioning for a role on an entirely different

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.319
series when she landed the now-iconic part
of Cheryl Blossom on Riverdale.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.400
Petsch, who says she caught the performing
bug at the age of three, was meeting with

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.180
casting director David Rappaport for The CW
series Legends of Tomorrow when he pinned

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:41.900
her for Cheryl.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.019
Although she was still fairly new to acting
at the time, Petsch had still boasted appearances

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.140
in the Nickelodeon series Instant Mom and
the fantasy flick The Curse of Sleeping Beauty.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.689
Plus, she played a key role in a national
Coca-Cola billboard advertising campaign in

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:56.120
the summer of 2014.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.420
Ashleigh Murray

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.760
Ashleigh Murray never ceases to steal a scene
— so it's pretty shocking to hear how little

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.360
experience the talented actress had before
landing the role of Pussycats bandleader Josie.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:11.840
Murray's few credits before Riverdale include
bit parts in episodes of The Following and

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.520
Younger as well as roles in the shorts Finding
Harmony, Welcome to New York, and Grind.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.760
Success came quickly for Murray after she
landed her role on Riverdale with a leading

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:26.100
role in the Sundance Film Festival breakout
Deidra and Laney Rob a Train in early 2017.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.220
Luke Perry

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.980
Former teen hunk Luke Perry already had a
lot of experience on teen shows when he signed

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:37.720
on to appear as Archie's dad Fred on Riverdale,
starring on the wildly popular Beverly Hills,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.560
90210 for nine years.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.220
During his time on 90210, Perry also made
the rounds in film and television, appearing

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.370
in the movie version of Buffy the Vampire
Slayer and starring in other flicks like The

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.040
Fifth Element and 8 Seconds.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.600
He also made guest appearances on an extensive
list of shows like Will and Grace, What I

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:59.310
Like About You, Leverage, Community, Body
of Proof, Raising Hope, Major Crimes, and

00:04:59.310 --> 00:04:59.960
Criminal Minds.

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:04.080
The actor has said he was "skeptical" about
making his return to television when Riverdale

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:08.039
came along, but, luckily, his agent pushed
him to read the script, and — just like

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.840
the show's devotees — he was hooked.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.140
Molly Ringwald

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.980
After landing a teen heartthrob to play Archie's
father, it makes sense that Riverdale's producers

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.480
would seek out another huge star to play his
mother.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:25.040
Enter Molly Ringwald, a venerable icon since
the 1980s and everybody's first redhead crush.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:30.320
Ringwald's many — many — film roles during
her "Brat Pack" teen-star days include Sixteen

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.900
Candles, The Breakfast Club, and Pretty in
Pink.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.139
Early on in her career, she also appeared
in various TV series like Diff'rent Strokes

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.060
and The Facts of Life.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.820
Ringwald's stepped out of the spotlight since
the '80s, but she still pops up on the big

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.940
screen every now and then.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.770
She was also a series regular on ABC Family's
The Secret Life of the American Teenager,

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:52.520
and she booked guest appearances on Medium
and Psych along with a lead role in the Canadian

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.320
series Raising Expectations.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.220
Mädchen Amick

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.500
Playing the Betty's mother, Alice Cooper — no,
not that Alice Cooper — Mädchen Amick is

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.760
another one of Riverdale's resident creepy
parents with a pretty impressive acting past.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.159
Most notable is her role as the waitress Shelley
Johnson on David Lynch's supernatural mystery

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:15.289
Twin Peaks, a role that she reprised in the
1992 prequel film Fire Walk With Me and the

00:06:15.289 --> 00:06:18.540
cult hit's 2017 reboot Twin Peaks: The Return.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.580
Amick's popped up here and there in a ton
of big-name shows since, from American Horror

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.020
Story to Gilmore Girls.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:29.020
But viewers may also recognize her from her
recurring roles in Central Park West, Freddie,

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.040
and Witches of East End.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.380
Marisol Nichols

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.040
Marisol Nichols has been conniving and cutthroat
in her role as Veronica's mother Hermione

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:40.520
Lodge, but she's also brought a lot of sensitivity
to the serious part.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.760
This is thanks to Nichols' long-time experience
in the acting business, which kicked off in

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:50.420
1996 with guest appearances on the short-lived
sitcom My Guys and Beverly Hills, 90210.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:54.780
Like many of her adult Riverdale co-stars,
Nichols was once a teen fixture in well-known

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.560
movies like Can't Hardly Wait, Vegas Vacation,
and Scream 2.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:03.360
She's also appeared on TV in a number of fan-favorite
shows like Charmed, Friends, and Boy Meets

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.900
World, before hitting it big on Fox's 24,
playing Special Agent Nadia Yassir.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.180
Mark Consuelos

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:15.260
Cast as Veronica's intense father Hiram Lodge
in Riverdale's second season, Mark Consuelos

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:20.360
started acting in 1995 when he starred in
the soap opera All My Children until 2010.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.560
In fact, that's where he met his wife, TV
host Kelly Ripa!

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.980
During that time, he also booked dozens of
other acting gigs, including guest-starring

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.160
roles on shows like Friends, American Family,
and Third Watch.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.880
He's also appeared in shows like Ugly Betty,
Law and Order: Special Victims Unit, and American

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.100
Horror Story: Asylum.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.400
Talk about a well-rounded CV!

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.500
Skeet Ulrich

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:46.220
Another former teen star recruited to play
a Riverdale parent, Skeet Ulrich was so impressive

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:50.650
as Jughead's criminal father FP in season
one that he was bumped up to a series regular

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.940
for season two — despite his character's
incarceration that is.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.210
He started off his acting career with small
uncredited roles in Weekend at Bernie's and

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.580
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles before breaking
out with a performance in the movie The Craft.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:07.680
Though horror hounds will likely recognize
him as villain Billy Loomis in 1996's Scream.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:12.460
During the '90s, he also had roles in Boys,
Ride with the Devil, and As Good as it Gets.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:16.379
Ulrich stayed in the spotlight in the next
decade as well, appearing on the TV series

00:08:16.379 --> 00:08:20.900
Into the West, Miracles, and Jericho, and
later guest starring in CSI: New York and

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.920
Law and Order: LA.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.160
Martin Cummins

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:29.540
Actor Martin Cummins, who plays the dead serious
Sheriff Keller, has the experience necessary

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.570
for a show where everyone is suspect — he's
held more than 75 credits stretching back

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.360
to 1987, after all.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.940
Although Cummins didn't achieve the same kind
of 1990s relevance as some of his co-stars,

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:44.090
he was a vital player in a lot of different
TV shows and movies, ranging from 21 Jump

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.980
Street to Highlander to Born to Run.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:50.760
In the late '90s, Cummins signed on to appear
in sci-fi smash Stargate SG-1.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:56.140
This move gave him the geek cred to later
show up in Smallville, and Kyle XY, and Bates

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:56.640
Motel.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.640
Lochlyn Munro

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.160
OK, so Betty's dad Hal Cooper isn't the most
congenial of Riverdale's grownups.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:07.680
But the actor who plays him, Lochlyn Munro,
seems like a perfectly nice guy — and a

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.160
busy one, with over 200 credits to his name.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.080
Munro hasn't had many parts that stuck around
for long, but he has been a prolific guest

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:19.780
star, appearing on shows like Charmed, Psych,
Bones, Lucifer, and Supernatural.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.920
While he's no stranger to T.V., Munro's probably
more well-known for his many film roles, which

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:30.090
come from a variety of genres, from campy
horror flicks like Freddy vs. Jason to comedies

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.060
like Scary Movie and Daddy Day Camp.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.760
Thanks for watching!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:38.310
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

